hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18218","Yazid ibn Abd Rabbih narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hassan al-Kinani that al-Harith ibn Muslim ibn al-Harith al-Tamimi narrated to him from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: When you pray the morning prayer, say before speaking to anyone: O Allah, protect me from the Fire, seven times, for if you die on that day Allah Almighty will decree for you protection from the Fire. And when you pray the sunset prayer, say before speaking to anyone: O Allah, I ask You for Paradise, O Allah, protect me from the Fire, seven times, for if you die on that night Allah Almighty will decree for you protection from the Fire."
"18219","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Hassan al-Kinani narrated to us from al-Harith ibn Muslim ibn al-Harith al-Tamimi from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote for him a written instruction to those after him among the rulers, and sealed it."
